    "    \"Quick usage guide:\\n\\n1) Create manager and object:\\n   mgr = ObjectManager()\\n   player = SpriteObject(\\\"player\\\", \\\"test2.png\\\", x=100, y=100)\\n\\n2) Add animations (must provide frame indices):\\n   player.add_frames(\\\"walk\\\", indices=[0,1,2,3,4,5,6], cols=3, rows=3, frame_duration=100, loop=True)\\n   player.add_frames(\\\"attack\\\", indices=[7,8,9], cols=3, rows=3, frame_duration=120, loop=False)\\n\\n3) Register and play:\\n   mgr.add(player)\\n   mgr.play(\\\"player\\\", \\\"walk\\\")\\n\\n4) Game loop:\\n   dt = clock.tick(60)\\n   mgr.update_all(dt)\\n   mgr.draw_all(screen)\\n\\n5) Helpers:\\n   mgr.is_finished(\\\"player\\\")  # check finish\\n   player.set_position(x,y) / player.move(dx,dy)\\n   player.add_frame_to_animation(\\\"attack\\\", pygame.Rect(x,y,w,h), duration=100)\\n\"\n",
